Write the application lists in one stable order

CFG_WRITE_STRING_LIST_ENTRY joins the values of a QSet. Qt seeds the
hash of a QSet for each process, so the nine application lists reach the
file in a different order on each start. The set the style builds does
not change, but the stored file changes with no user edit. Two exports
of one unchanged configuration therefore differ.

Sort the list before the join. The dialog already sorts the same list
for display, so the file now holds the order the user sees.

Six processes that write one list of five names give six orders before
the change and one order after it.

The change sits on the branch work/config-io of the local tree, as commit 2 of 18.
A new merge request on system/qtcurve takes that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

diff --git a/qt6/common/config_file.cpp b/qt6/common/config_file.cpp
index ee4c4b59..17a4e735 100644
--- a/qt6/common/config_file.cpp
+++ b/qt6/common/config_file.cpp
@@ -2237,11 +2237,15 @@ static const char * toStr(ETBarBtn tb)
         CFG.writeEntry(#ENTRY ".pos", (int)(opts.ENTRY.pos)); \
     }
 
-#define CFG_WRITE_STRING_LIST_ENTRY(ENTRY) \
-    if (!exportingStyle && def.ENTRY==opts.ENTRY) \
-        CFG.deleteEntry(#ENTRY); \
-    else \
-        CFG.writeEntry(#ENTRY, QStringList(opts.ENTRY.values()).join(",")); \
+#define CFG_WRITE_STRING_LIST_ENTRY(ENTRY) do {                 \
+        if (!exportingStyle && def.ENTRY==opts.ENTRY) {         \
+            CFG.deleteEntry(#ENTRY);                            \
+        } else {                                                \
+            QStringList list(opts.ENTRY.values());              \
+            list.sort();                                        \
+            CFG.writeEntry(#ENTRY, list.join(","));             \
+        }                                                       \
+    } while (0)
 
 bool qtcWriteConfig(KConfig *cfg, const Options &opts, const Options &def, bool exportingStyle)
 {
